gle layers across slatted wooden racks on the sunny back porch to harden their skins in the afternoon sun.","byline":null,"source":"projects","reason":"harvest progress report","carry":null,"date":"2026-10-16","published":true,"draftedByStub":false,"state":"published","submittedAt":"2026-10-16T09:30:00.004Z","publishedAt":"2026-10-16T09:30:00.004Z","createdAt":"2026-10-16T09:30:00.004Z","updatedAt":"2026-10-16T09:30:00.004Z","revision":1,"copyId":"copy-ddc26fcb-1176-4e81-93b2-4278528e9387","copyDigest":"c84bd197579ffbaec3c044a5c83e576ba3b9f6277c1c7b189194456f9066e965","bylineName":null,"outsideText":false,"sourceReference":null,"withdrawnAt":null,"withdrawnBy":null},{"slug":"2026-10-16-county-tax-inquiry-window-opens-f7ed86c0","edition":160,"kind":"report","title":"County tax inquiry window opens","standfirst":null,"body":"The annual property tax assessment letter sits in the inbox, giving residents thirty days to review the revised building and woodlot valuation. Nora plans to compare the listed square footage against the tax maps on Tuesday before filing the paperwork in the attic deed box.","byline":null,"source":"the inbox","reason":"notice due, in the inbox","carry":null,"date":"2026-10-16","published":true,"draftedByStub":false,"state":"published","submittedAt":"2026-10-16T09:30:00.004Z","publishedAt":"2026-10-16T09:30:00.004Z","createdAt":"2026-10-16T09:30:00.004Z","updatedAt":"2026-10-16T09:30:00.004Z","revision":1,"copyId":"copy-084ba4d4-b774-4429-aaba-9aed9ad02fcd","copyDigest":"15d6e48e38a1e9a8f0f6551650ef7980afffb23f090caa0843d3db8330126cb0","bylineName":null,"outsideText":false,"sourceReference":null,"withdrawnAt":null,"withdrawnBy":null}],"sky":{"clock":{"offsetMinutes":-240},"season":"autumn","instant":"2026-10-16T09:30:00.000Z","sun":{"rise":"2026-10-16T11:21:41.664Z","set":"2026-10-16T22:23:06.917Z","altitude":-20.747827826585176,"polar":null,"local":{"set":"18:23"}},"moon":{"fraction":0.2924644164084405,"waxing":true,"parallacticAngle":-7.226092714